{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/LetToHave.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.letToHave\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">Sym</span>.<span class=\"name\">letToHave</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Sym/SymM.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM\">SymM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Converts the nondependent `let` declarations of `e` into `have` declarations. The\nresult is definitionally equal to `e`, has the same shape (only `nondep` flags change),\nand is maximally shared. If nothing is converted, the result is pointer-equal to `e`\n(check with `isSameExpr`).\n\nAssumptions: `e` is maximally shared, has no loose bound variables, and is type\ncorrect. Metavariables are treated as opaque values.\n","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Sym/LetToHave.html#Lean.Meta.Sym.letToHave","kind":"def","line":393,"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.letToHave","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/470d5ce1400764999581fd26d5d72b00d990b0f4/src/Lean/Meta/Sym/LetToHave.lean#L393-L414"}}],"imports":["Lean.Meta.Sym.AlphaShareBuilder","Lean.Meta.Sym.InferType","Lean.Meta.Sym.ReplaceS","Lean.Meta.Sym.SymM"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Meta.Sym.LetToHave"}